  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is zero, so ${f}^{\u2032}(2)=0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is negative, so ${f}^{\u2032}(3)<0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=6$ is positive, so ${f}^{\u2032}(6)>0.$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{\u2032}(3)<{f}^{\u2032}(2)<{f}^{\u2032}(6).$",
